From: chopin postmarketOS bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] output-shield: dispose animation before its rectangle

Disposing a playing timed animation skips it to completion and emits done.
The shield's done callback calls stop_render(), which still needs color_rect.
Clearing color_rect first makes that callback pass NULL to phoc_bling_unmap()
and abort the compositor when a pending shield animation is torn down after
the userspace freezer thaws. Dispose the animation while its target is alive.

--- a/src/output-shield.c
+++ b/src/output-shield.c
@@ -209,10 +209,10 @@ phoc_output_shield_finalize (GObject *object)
   set_output (self, NULL);
   stop_render (self);
 
+  g_clear_object (&self->animation);
   g_clear_object (&self->color_rect);
   g_clear_object (&self->easer);
-  g_clear_object (&self->animation);
   g_clear_object (&self->spinner);
 
   G_OBJECT_CLASS (phoc_output_shield_parent_class)->finalize (object);
 }
